reports.summary:
I checked all seven claims against their measurements and run records and found each supported within its narrowed scope. The checks covered:
- all six arm means and SDs;
- the per-seed paired deltas against off_policy_ref;
- the fixed-switch sign counts;
- the self-reported switch steps, forced_switch values and on-policy batch counts, where on_policy_batches equals 3000 minus switch_step on every seed.

The falsification reading is consistent with the registered falsification outcome (1): pure_on_policy has the lower mean.

The setup statements match prepare.py@v1 and train.py@v1–v5, the frozen protocol environment and the profile. Their content covers the task, metric, fold construction, models, teacher training, loss, optimiser, batch size, steps, sampling, probe seeding, the trigger and cap, yoked seeding, corruption seeding, budget, the registered prediction and falsification, and the analysis. Together these are sufficient to rerun the study.

The related-work statements are consistent with the cited abstracts.

I record one minor note that does not block release, about the scope wording of claim_adaptive_not_below_pure_on. No previous issues were assigned to this lens.
